Package: mcnemarOR
Type: Package
Title: Paired Samples Contingency Tables, with Odds Ratio and Agreement
Version: 0.1.0
Date: 2026-08-22
Authors@R: c(person("Ravi", "Selker", role=c("aut", "cph")),
    person("Jonathon", "Love", role=c("aut", "cph"), email="jon@thon.cc"),
    person("Damian", "Dropmann", role=c("aut", "cph")),
    person("Victor", "Moreno", role=c("aut", "cre", "cph"), email="v.moreno@iconcologia.net"),
    person("Maurizio", "Agosti", role=c("ctb", "cph")),
    person("Sebastian", "Jentschke", role=c("ctb", "cph")))
Maintainer: Victor Moreno <v.moreno@iconcologia.net>
Description: A clone of jmv's Paired Samples Contingency Tables (McNemar test) analysis,
    restructured to separate hypothesis tests from comparative measures (mirroring
    'conttables2xK'), and extended with: a paired odds ratio (b/c) and a difference in
    paired proportions, both with confidence intervals, for 2x2 tables; an optional exact
    odds ratio (conditional MLE with exact confidence interval); an exact McNemar test
    based on the binomial distribution; marginal percentages in the frequency table;
    observed agreement and Cohen's kappa; and, for RxR tables (R > 2), Bowker's test of
    symmetry and the Stuart-Maxwell test of marginal homogeneity, the natural
    generalizations of McNemar's test and the difference in proportions test respectively.
    This package is intended for use from the 'jamovi' statistical spreadsheet (see
    <https://www.jamovi.org> for more information).
BugReports: https://github.com/jamovi/jmv/issues
